## Summary

Simplicity audit of main at 8e7b9f76. The tree was already in good shape on the open cleanup issues (sexp lists derive isList; geocode lookups are one record). The audit collapsed four real duplications and left the rest because the copies are different rules.

Built: one setPicture in web/common/images.js for Home, Team, and Celebrate (post a photo, then delete the previous one). One andList in web/common/andlist.js for the English "A, B and C" lists that had been copied in the calendar, parties, and the When event page. Home's parseDate and tint live once in web/home/state.js, shared by the month view and widgets. queueCount no longer stores Done; JSON derives done as 0 when total is 0 and total minus pending otherwise, including nested parts.

Decisions: andList is its own leaf module so the calendar does not import person tiles. Home's date parser was not switched to parseWhen, which returns null on a bad string. When's setPicture stayed, because it posts only when a file was chosen and deletes the event's current photo. Queue done keeps the old zero-total case so sign-in and sweep JSON do not go negative.

Left out: school-year start versus Staff Birthdays' year start, HMAC signers for different tokens, the two PDF thumbnail walks, When versus Home availability wording, the server's mail joinNames, and single-implementation store interfaces. Review found nothing to change. Merging main added only a log line in tools/pdfthumbnails when a PDF's pages are reused; that combined cleanly.

